wh40k-class-specialization-operative-techno-adept-name = Mysteries of the Machine Spirit
wh40k-class-specialization-operative-techno-adept-description = Diagnostics, repair, and temporary safe machine interactions.

wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-01-name = Rite of the Machine Spirit
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-01-description = Unlocks the technical stance. Bonuses require a suitable tool and a device explicitly tagged for hacking or service.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-02-name = Tactile Diagnostics
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-02-description = Examining a device shows its power, panel, damage, and available actions. Private player data and container contents remain hidden.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-03-name = Sacred Contact
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-03-description = Shortens ordinary panel, repair, and wiring service while preserving every tool and access check.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-04-name = Machine Whisper
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-04-description = Briefly reveals nearby visible permitted technical objects and basic condition. It cannot see through walls or scan inventories.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-05-name = Lock Bypass
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-05-description = Starts a noisy DoAfter at a visible wh40k-hackable door and temporarily opens only an unbolted door. Permanent access lists never change.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-06-name = Wiring Path
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-06-description = At an open panel, reveals one safe wiring clue to reduce mistakes without exposing the entire randomized wire layout.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-07-name = Safety Shunt
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-07-description = Temporarily places a permitted device in a safe powered-down state for service. It neither disables vital systems nor creates energy.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-08-name = Field Repair
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-08-description = Uses a real held repair kit on suitable machinery, barricades, or deployed weapons. Tool resources are consumed and destroyed objects stay destroyed.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-09-name = Cogitator Trail
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-09-description = After successful diagnostics, remembers a nearby visible device of the same type and its direction within a short range.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-10-name = Silent Breaker
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-10-description = Temporarily unbolts one permitted door after hacking its open panel. It automatically reverts and fails in protected zones.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-11-name = Tool Discipline
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-11-description = The first service action after changing devices is faster; it excludes door hacking and never removes the DoAfter.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-12-name = Repairer's Beacon
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-12-description = Deploys a small light or diagnostic beacon from a real consumable. It highlights damaged permitted machinery and is not a turret.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-13-name = Technical Bulwark
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-13-description = Barricades and barbed wire placed or repaired by the Operative remain functional longer; unrelated construction gains nothing.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-14-name = Circuit Loop
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-14-description = Temporarily disables one unprotected sensor or alarm after hacking, while the intervention remains in the server log.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-15-name = Servitor Arm
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-15-description = Reduces the speed penalty when carrying a suitable large technical item without increasing inventory capacity.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-16-name = Command Protocol
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-16-description = Briefly shows the group a hacked passage or dangerous device visible to the Operative, with a timer.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-17-name = Coded Key
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-17-description = After two different successful service actions on one device, the next permitted hack is faster. It does not stack and failure resets it.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-18-name = Quell the Machine's Wrath
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-18-description = Temporarily suppresses a dangerous mode on permitted automated machinery so the group can retreat or repair. Each machinery category needs an explicit interface; players are unaffected.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-19-name = Sanctioned Intrusion
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-19-description = A long visible hack briefly opens one protected but explicitly permitted passage or terminal. The server checks zone, owner, target, and combat restrictions.
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-20-name = Voice of the Omnissiah
wh40k-class-skill-operative-techno-adept-20-description = Final node: improves diagnostics, service, and temporary bypasses through one capped modifier. It grants no permanent access, remote hacking, or access to forbidden objects.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeMachineWhisper = machine whisper
    .desc = Privately inspect an explicitly sanctioned nearby device.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeLockBypass = lock bypass
    .desc = Start a noisy interruptible bypass on an unbolted sanctioned door.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeSafetyShunt = safety shunt
    .desc = Temporarily disable a sanctioned device after an interruptible service action.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeFieldRepair = field repair
    .desc = Repair structural damage using one real held cable resource.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeQuietBreaker = quiet breaker
    .desc = Temporarily release bolts on a sanctioned door with its panel open.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeRepairBeacon = repair beacon
    .desc = Inspect a sanctioned visible damaged device.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeCircuitLoop = circuit loop
    .desc = Temporarily isolate a sanctioned device with an open panel.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeCommandProtocol = command protocol
    .desc = Privately report the state of a sanctioned visible device.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeMachineWrath = calm machine wrath
    .desc = Temporarily place a sanctioned automatic device into a safe state.
ent-ActionWh40kOperativeSanctionedHack = sanctioned hack
    .desc = Perform a long visible temporary bypass with full server revalidation.

wh40k-class-device-scan-result = { $device }: structural damage { $damage }, bolts down: { $bolts }.
